</dl>
<div class="postbody">
<div id="post_content1119420">
<h3 class="first">
<a href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/viewtopic.php?p=1119420&amp;#p1119420">HiRez scanning duty (**Completed!**)</a>
</h3>
<ul class="post-buttons">
<li>
<a class="button button-icon-only" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=1119420" title="Reply with quote">
<i aria-hidden="true" class="icon fa-quote-left fa-fw"></i><span class="sr-only">Quote</span>
</a>
</li>
<li class="responsive-menu hidden dropdown-container"><a class="js-responsive-menu-link responsive-menu-link dropdown-toggle"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon fa-bars fa-fw"></i></a><div class="dropdown"><div class="pointer"><div class="pointer-inner"></div></div><ul class="dropdown-contents"></ul></div></li></ul>
<p class="author">
<a class="unread" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/viewtopic.php?p=1119420&amp;#p1119420" title="Post">
<i aria-hidden="true" class="icon fa-file fa-fw icon-lightgray icon-md"></i><span class="sr-only">Post</span>
</a>
<span class="responsive-hide">by <strong><a class="username" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=16658">strangewayes</a></strong> » </span><time datetime="2017-05-20T14:02:31+00:00">May 20th, 2017, 10:02 am</time>
</p>
<div class="content">All cards have been scanned. Virtual cards are currently being implemented. Errata to follow.<br/>
<br/>
Download Links:<br/>
I have updated the google drive to have a master folder so I can just share one link. You will find all the respective folders here:<br/>
<a class="postlink" href="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/12i00KRLriVraozX2i8MVLKHm4HJnQPB0?usp=sharing">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/ ... sp=sharing</a><br/>
-------------------<br/>
<br/>
Hello all,<br/>
<br/>
I was enraptured with the SWCCG when it came out. However, being 12 at the time, I lacked the resources to participate. By the time I was old enough to gather the funds, the game had already been shut down, and life was speeding up. Now, over 20 years later, I've gotten back into it with my girlfriend and we were both excited and disappointed to find that there are scans of all the cards we might need, but they're terrible in quality.<br/>
<br/>
Being a retired graphic designer with a masters degree, I have some serious scanning and computer equipment! I've got the time, motivation, and ability to put together an entire 600dpi SWCCG image archive. I've contacted a few people I've found with complete collections, but haven't heard back from them yet. I'm willing to spend the time scanning, adjusting, and hosting every single card in the SWCCG, so we have access to them forever. It would be a major boon for the community. I'm willing to do all the work just so I can have them myself, so I can imagine there are quite a few of you out there who would also enjoy a set of scans!<br/>
<br/>
Does anyone here have access to a complete collection and is willing to discuss tackling this project with me? Thank you!<br/>
<br/>
**Update 2-21-2023**<br/>
<br/>
If you're new to this thread, there is currently a crew cleaning up these scans for a massive remaster project that will include all card sets and virtual card sets. They are taking the last steps to preserve and finalize everything in areas where I could not. Please be aware, I am not in control of that project, nor do I participate in it. While I continue to follow along with the progress of this game, I am not a resource for access to newer versions of these cards. I will, however, continue to maintain the above download links unless there is a time where they are no longer useful/needed.<br/>
<br/>
Thank you to everyone who is working on that project. It's exactly what I, and many, many others were hoping for.</div>
<div class="notice">
					Last edited by <a class="username" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=16658">strangewayes</a> on February 21st, 2023, 3:38 pm, edited 27 times in total.
									</div>
