<div class="postbody">
<div id="post_content1119498">
<h3>
<a href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/viewtopic.php?p=1119498&amp;#p1119498">Re: Volunteering for HiRez scanning duty</a>
</h3>
<ul class="post-buttons">
<li>
<a class="button button-icon-only" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=1119498" title="Reply with quote">
<i aria-hidden="true" class="icon fa-quote-left fa-fw"></i><span class="sr-only">Quote</span>
</a>
</li>
<li class="responsive-menu hidden dropdown-container"><a class="js-responsive-menu-link responsive-menu-link dropdown-toggle"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon fa-bars fa-fw"></i></a><div class="dropdown"><div class="pointer"><div class="pointer-inner"></div></div><ul class="dropdown-contents"></ul></div></li></ul>
<p class="author">
<a class="unread" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/viewtopic.php?p=1119498&amp;#p1119498" title="Post">
<i aria-hidden="true" class="icon fa-file fa-fw icon-lightgray icon-md"></i><span class="sr-only">Post</span>
</a>
<span class="responsive-hide">by <strong><a class="username" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=16658">strangewayes</a></strong> » </span><time datetime="2017-05-21T03:30:26+00:00">May 20th, 2017, 11:30 pm</time>
</p>
<div class="content">Please don't bother trying to discredit me, Remaker. I've just started playing the game again after over twenty years and haven't had an account until now. According to you, I should spend years posting and interacting with the community before suggesting such a task? This is days upon days worth of work I'm willing to do for free, and you're going to attempt to make me out as a villain?<br/>
<br/>
I own an eBay top rated seller store with 3800 positive feedback. My name is James. I live in Omaha. If anyone is interested in working with me, I'd be more than willing to provide them with the rest of my information, phone number, address, and more. I'm also willing to have legal documents drafted to prevent me from 'stealing their collection' if they so choose. No one would be willing to work with me until I discuss the 'how' with them - I feel that should have been obvious. I'm well aware of what an entire collection of SWCCG cards are worth, otherwise I would have already purchased a set of my own to scan - there are several on eBay right now for sale at $3000+.<br/>
<br/>
I'm trying to aid the community. You've already disqualified yourself as someone without a complete set, so please just move along.</div>
</div>
</div>
