<div class="post has-profile bg1" id="p1119520">
<div class="inner">
<dl class="postprofile" id="profile1119520">
<dt class="has-profile-rank has-avatar">
<div class="avatar-container">
<a class="avatar" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=16658"><img alt="User avatar" class="avatar" height="100" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="100"/></a> </div>
<a class="username" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=16658">strangewayes</a> </dt>
<dd class="profile-rank">Member</dd>
<dd class="profile-posts"><strong>Posts:</strong> <a href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/search.php?author_id=16658&amp;sr=posts">94</a></dd> <dd class="profile-joined"><strong>Joined:</strong> May 20th, 2017, 9:52 am</dd>
</dl>
<div class="postbody">
<div id="post_content1119520">
<h3>
<a href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/viewtopic.php?p=1119520&amp;#p1119520">Re: Volunteering for HiRez scanning duty</a>
</h3>
<ul class="post-buttons">
<li>
<a class="button button-icon-only" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=1119520" title="Reply with quote">
<i aria-hidden="true" class="icon fa-quote-left fa-fw"></i><span class="sr-only">Quote</span>
</a>
</li>
<li class="responsive-menu hidden dropdown-container"><a class="js-responsive-menu-link responsive-menu-link dropdown-toggle"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon fa-bars fa-fw"></i></a><div class="dropdown"><div class="pointer"><div class="pointer-inner"></div></div><ul class="dropdown-contents"></ul></div></li></ul>
<p class="author">
<a class="unread" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/viewtopic.php?p=1119520&amp;#p1119520" title="Post">
<i aria-hidden="true" class="icon fa-file fa-fw icon-lightgray icon-md"></i><span class="sr-only">Post</span>
</a>
<span class="responsive-hide">by <strong><a class="username" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=16658">strangewayes</a></strong> » </span><time datetime="2017-05-21T13:56:25+00:00">May 21st, 2017, 9:56 am</time>
</p>
<div class="content">That's a great idea Floris! I went ahead and posted in the player locator forum under the appropriate location.<br/>
<br/>
I have five different scanners to use, and I've tried them all on the cards. My Mustek A3F2400N 2400dpi/48-bit scanner seems to pick up the best color, contrast, and detail on the cards. As you said, the results almost look surreally accurate in areas when comparing the actual card with my eyeballs. Just makes me more excited to do this!<br/>
<br/>
If I cannot find anyone with a complete set, I'll eventually start buying sets one expansion at a time to scan. But I'll have to buy one, scan it, wait for it to sell again on eBay, and then move on to another. Funds are pretty tight right now. I'd also lose out on having access to all the promos and odds &amp; ends that most people have picked up over the years.</div>
</div>
</div>
