<div class="post has-profile bg1" id="p1119558">
<div class="inner">
<dl class="postprofile" id="profile1119558">
<dt class="has-profile-rank has-avatar">
<div class="avatar-container">
<a class="avatar" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=16658"><img alt="User avatar" class="avatar" height="100" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="100"/></a> </div>
<a class="username" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=16658">strangewayes</a> </dt>
<dd class="profile-rank">Member</dd>
<dd class="profile-posts"><strong>Posts:</strong> <a href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/search.php?author_id=16658&amp;sr=posts">94</a></dd> <dd class="profile-joined"><strong>Joined:</strong> May 20th, 2017, 9:52 am</dd>
</dl>
<div class="postbody">
<div id="post_content1119558">
<h3>
<a href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/viewtopic.php?p=1119558&amp;#p1119558">Re: Volunteering for HiRez scanning duty</a>
</h3>
<ul class="post-buttons">
<li>
<a class="button button-icon-only" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=1119558" title="Reply with quote">
<i aria-hidden="true" class="icon fa-quote-left fa-fw"></i><span class="sr-only">Quote</span>
</a>
</li>
<li class="responsive-menu hidden dropdown-container"><a class="js-responsive-menu-link responsive-menu-link dropdown-toggle"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon fa-bars fa-fw"></i></a><div class="dropdown"><div class="pointer"><div class="pointer-inner"></div></div><ul class="dropdown-contents"></ul></div></li></ul>
<p class="author">
<a class="unread" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/viewtopic.php?p=1119558&amp;#p1119558" title="Post">
<i aria-hidden="true" class="icon fa-file fa-fw icon-lightgray icon-md"></i><span class="sr-only">Post</span>
</a>
<span class="responsive-hide">by <strong><a class="username" href="https://forum.starwarsccg.org/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=16658">strangewayes</a></strong> » </span><time datetime="2017-05-21T20:52:49+00:00">May 21st, 2017, 4:52 pm</time>
</p>
<div class="content"><blockquote><div><cite>AdmiralMotti89 wrote:</cite>I live in Hastings (just a couple hours west of you) and have at least one complete set of everything.</div></blockquote>

I certainly don't mind making the trip out to see you then! I'll PM you about that. That's fantastic luck!<br/>
<blockquote><div><cite>AdmiralMotti89 wrote:</cite>Are you trying to get scans of both foils and originals? WB and BB? AI and regular? Sorry if this was already mentioned and I missed it.</div></blockquote>

If people are interested in having all options - and I suspect they will want them - I think its the proper thing to do it right and scan both versions. Is a foil version something someone would want to print? I'm not entirely sure what they'll look like when scanned, but I suspect they'll have a blue or green haze across them and just appear more or less 'bad'.<br/>
<blockquote><div><cite>AdmiralMotti89 wrote:</cite>If you are not looking to scan literally every card, what about Pre-2.0 cards (Special Edition) that were later foiled and thus had corrected text?</div></blockquote>

I'm willing to scan 'everything' to make sure this is done right. I will address the corrected text below.<br/>
<blockquote><div><cite>AdmiralMotti89 wrote:</cite>The other thing to consider is that while the PC images might not be glorious quality, it looks like they have been updated with the correct (post-errata) text. By looking at the Decipher Errata slips pdf, it looks like there are about 500 cards with official text different from the card itself. Just something to consider while thinking about going to all this work; a significant percentage of card texts won't be correct.</div></blockquote>

All of the Errata slips are of perfect quality and really aren't that big of a deal to overlay onto the 'old version' of the cards that I scan. It will be a project in and of itself, but lets face it, it needs to be done if I'm going to make scans available. I'd rather scan the old cards and overlay the errata onto them so they look correct than just scan the foil ones, which I'm dubious about.</div>
</div>
</div>
