<div class="content"><blockquote><div><cite>AdmiralMotti89 wrote:</cite><blockquote><div><cite>Munchanka wrote:</cite>For their commendable archival efforts, Motti and Strangewayes should get custom v-card characters as Imperial archivists at the Citadel Tower on Scarif.</div></blockquote>

I already know what my text is going to be: <br/>
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Once per game, examine the cards in your reserve deck, reorder however you wish, and replace; change your mind on how you ordered them, take them out of the sleeves altogether and put them into different art sleeves that fit the theme of your deck better; then take those out of the sleeves again and try to shoehorn the basic character pattern into a completely different objective; buy more ink cartridges; set aside 15 of the v-slips you printed out and then print out 15 new ones to fit your new objective; reshuffle.</div></blockquote></div></blockquote>

I love it. The whole spoof v slips never got off the ground but this would be so good for that.</div>
<div class="signature" id="sig1119593">* Congrats if you read through my whole post. Have a cookie, it's in your cache.<br/>
* <a class="postlink" href="https://gemp.starwarsccg.org/gemp-swccg">https://gemp.starwarsccg.org/gemp-swccg</a> Play for free, even if you don't own good cards. Then play in real life, with real people, even if you aren't any good.<br/>
<img alt="Image" class="postimage" src="data:image/jpeg;base64,"/> <img alt="Image" class="postimage" src="data:image/jpeg;base64,"/> <img alt="Image" class="postimage" src="data:image/jpeg;base64,"/>
<blockquote><div><cite>Sagnet wrote:</cite>At this point, I think your posts are more unclear than the rules are. </div></blockquote></div>
</div>
</div>
